      "title": "Re-creating a compound card while one of its parts is trashed",
      "reason": "Ruby looks for a trashed junction to revive before it has resolved the revived part's id, finds none, and inserts a second cards row for the same (left_id, right_id) pair. That insert only succeeds on the oracle deck, which lacks the production schema's UNIQUE (left_id, right_id) index; on the production schema the same Ruby save fails. The TypeScript engine revives the existing trashed junction row instead (recording the revival's name, type, content, trash and part changes), which keeps one row per name and is valid on the production schema.",
